title The meter that swallowed its own instrument, and the fold that lost its depth
prompt The baton, seat grass. Lap N 4037 by git rev-list --count HEAD.
rota lap 4037, row 2 -- Fire, Mars, cut and stop, and its sense is vision. No lap on this shelf had read row 2 today, so no advance by hand was needed. Read the threshold and all three seats: Standfast, reds-first, the three depths of removal. The row asks a lap to look straight at the thing it would rather route around and then act once at exactly the depth the truth requires, and it named this lap's whole subject before the cold pass finished.
think Round-open read the tree first. git stash list held one entry -- fleet-round-open 20260906-072758, a lap's unsent work, twelve files -- and the cold roster named it again on its own first lines, stashed_entries=1 with the detail. So the thing this lap would rather route around was announced twice before any guard ran.
think The cold pass took 840s over 134 guards and came back 129 green, 1 red, 4 gated. The red was standing_equipment, and its own scan said why in one word: runs_unrostered: copy_lag. The untracked run ledger held a green receipt for a guard at 20260906.070809 that the roster does not name, because the dead lap's stash had carried the roster line and all three files out of the tree while leaving the receipt behind.
think Read the stash before touching it. It held a finished, green lap of this seat's own lane -- copy_lag scan, control and witness, a REDS row, a roster entry, a card correction and its session log. Nothing about it was speculative; it had run.
think Then the fault, and it was inside the recovered work rather than around it. construction/standing-equipment-reds/instrument_refusal.txt, written 07:20:53, named tools/fixtures/c/copy_lag_scan.sh:58 as a swallowed instrument pass against a ceiling of zero, verdict=over_ceiling. A standing guard had refused, written its evidence, and been read by nobody for eighty minutes -- because the lap that would have read it was already dying, and because that evidence file is untracked by .gitignore:384.
think Two faults wore that one line. git ls-files piped into awk under || true is the swallow instrument_refusal gates; and the empty branch answered verdict=no_rye at exit 0, so a root that could not be read was indistinguishable from an honest tree with no Rye in it. The scan's own header three lines above declares the opposite -- both refuse rather than truncate, since a silently short reading is the fault this file exists to name.
think Repaired to the shape its sibling rye_compile_reach_scan.sh already carried: git ls-files refuses by name at verdict=no_checkout, the awk pass refuses at verdict=instrument_failed, and the empty corpus exits 2.
think A control that passes on its first run has not been proven able to make a sound. Planted the swallow alone, the exit-0 alone, the unnamed refusal alone, and the original form whole. Each plant is bitten by the leg that should bite it and by no other; under the whole original form all four new legs read no and instrument_refusal reproduces over_ceiling on the same line number.
think The row number had to move. The stash booked %469 and a peer published its own %469 while the work sat stashed, so the row renumbered to %472 keeping its 20260906.070240 stamp, per derived-spine's own worked repair. Read --next off the anointed spine after git fetch xy rather than off this tree.
obs THE EXIT-CODE LEG ALONE WOULD HAVE MISSED THE FAULT. Planting only the swallow leaves no_checkout_refuses reading yes, because a swallowed git refusal falls through to the empty branch, which also refuses. Only the verdict leg tells a refused checkout from a tree with no Rye in it. Two legs for what looked like one fault, and the decomposition is what makes the repair provable rather than plausible.
obs A GUARD'S REFUSAL IS WRITTEN WHERE NOTHING TRACKED CAN READ IT. instrument_refusal did everything right: it refused, it named the file and the line, it wrote the evidence. That evidence went to construction/standing-equipment-reds/, gitignored at line 384, so no commit carried it, no card mentioned it, and no peer could see it. It surfaced only because a different instrument -- standing_equipment reading its own untracked run ledger -- noticed a receipt whose guard had left the roster. A dying lap takes its own red with it, and this is the mechanism. Named on the card rather than taken; a repair reaches into how every guard records a refusal, which is wider than one lap.
obs A SECOND RED, FOUND BY GRADING WHAT I TOUCHED, AND IT FIRED ON ME WHILE I WROTE IT UP. The QA card on the shelf I had just written read truth_counted=80, one cited path unresolved: a link folded off construction/ITINERARY.md kept the card's own depth and landed one directory deeper. Swept the family -- five of eight itinerary-landed-accounts shelves, sixteen links. reds_fold.sh re-anchors exactly this when its loom folds a REDS row and proves shelf_links_one_level_short=0; the live front folds to the same directory by hand and nothing re-anchors. Three guards read that room and none reads this: tracked_link gates a link that resolves here and breaks in a clone, and these resolve nowhere; reds_fold reads only shelves its own loom wrote; readme_reach walks front doors. Repaired all sixteen, bounded to links resolving under exactly one of the two corrections a card-to-shelf fold can need, so nothing was guessed. Then it fired on three consecutive hand-folds inside this one lap -- the %467-%468 account folded to make room for the row, and the %451-%469 account folded again after the rebase -- eighteen instances, the last two written by the hand describing the mechanism. A property a hand cannot hold while actively thinking about it is a property that wants a program. %474 BOOKED: instances repaired, loom booked.
obs A THIRD RED, AND IT WAS THE ONE BLOCKING THE SEND. The hot pass refused with standing_equipment red while runs_unrostered read 0 -- the genuine fault was repaired and the guard refused anyway, on one line: red: standing_equipment red. It is itself rostered, so standing_equipment_run.sh writes its verdict into the run card standing_equipment_scan.sh then reads and counts. Its first red is therefore absorbing: the reading that produced it becomes the reading that reproduces it, with the tree perfectly repaired in between. Proven on metal with one variable -- that row present reads runs_red=1 verdict=roster_broken, that row alone removed reads runs_red=0 verdict=ok. A guard's own verdict is its output, never its evidence, and the loop stays invisible for exactly as long as the guard is green. Repaired to report at runs_red_self and never count, one name wide. Five control legs, and three plants: the exemption removed, the exemption aimed at a name that never matches, and a peer's red routed into the self counter -- the last takes peer_red_still_bites to no, which is the hole a careless exemption would actually leave. %475 CLOSED.
obs THREE REDS IN ONE LAP, EACH FOUND BY THE REPAIR OF THE ONE BEFORE IT. The stash recovery surfaced the swallowed instrument; grading the shelf that recovery needed surfaced the fold depth; and the hot pass that was to prove the first two surfaced the absorbing verdict. None was reachable from the card, and each was one command past the last. That is the Fire row's own claim -- a lap that looks straight at the thing it would rather route around finds the next thing behind it.
obs THE CARD WAS 130 BYTES OVER ITS CEILING BEFORE I WROTE A WORD. The recovered stash's own card edit put construction/ITINERARY.md at 41,090 against 40,960. Rather than raise a bound sized per ship, folded 1,224 bytes of finished account -- the withdrawn 41 orphans, the harness_roster landing, the three-firing lantern's spec -- verbatim onto a landed-accounts shelf, and left the OPEN %466 claim and the standing question on the card. A finished section folds; only living parts earn a raise.
obs THE ROSTER TOOK 840s FOR 134 GUARDS UNDER THIS HARNESS AND DID NOT DIE. The prior grass lap recorded three reproducible deaths at 15, 27 and 57 guards under this same harness, repaired by setsid nohup. This lap ran it as an ordinary background command and it completed, so whatever that was is not reproducing today. Recorded rather than explained; one clean run does not close a red that fired three times.
loom witness=copy_lag wall_s=8 pen_behaviors=31 tracked_rye=1941 basenames_both_ways=108 copies=5 behind=2 sibling=3
loom roster=cold_open guards=134 green=129 red=1 gated=4 wall_s=840
loom witness=instrument_refusal scans_read=717 swallowed=0 ceiling=0
loom sweep=itinerary_fold_shelves shelves=8 faulted=5 links_repaired=18 unresolved_after=0 hand_folds_this_lap=3 hand_folds_that_lost_depth=3
loom witness=standing_equipment legs_added=5 plants=3 runs_red=0 runs_red_self=1
file tools/fixtures/c/copy_lag_scan.sh the repair -- git and awk each refuse by name, and the empty corpus exits 2 rather than 0
file tools/fixtures/c/copy_lag_control.sh four legs added: empty_refuses, no_checkout_says_so, no_checkout_named, no_checkout_refuses -- 31 behaviors
file tools/co/copy_lag_witness.rish asserts the four new legs and says in its head what refuses before any reading happens
file construction/archive/REDS-the-copy-that-was-counted-against-itself-rows-472-473.md both rows, %469 renumbered to %472 against the anointed spine, %473 booked and closed on metal
file construction/ITINERARY.md the GRASS block carries both landings and the find handed over; 1,224 bytes of finished account folded off
file construction/archive/20260906-090312_itinerary-landed-accounts.md the shelf that fold went to, verbatim
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri copy_lag rostered at tier lap, which is what takes standing_equipment back to green
file construction/archive/REDS-a-fold-done-by-hand-loses-its-depth-rows-474.md %474 BOOKED -- sixteen links repaired, the seventeenth written by the hand describing the mechanism
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_scan.sh the self row reported at runs_red_self and never counted, so one red stops being absorbing
file tools/fixtures/s/standing_equipment_control.sh five legs, the exemption proven one name wide from both sides
file construction/archive/REDS-a-guard-that-reads-its-own-verdict-rows-475.md %475 CLOSED -- one variable on metal, that row present against that row removed
recommend keep-going -- the three reds this lap found are closed or booked, and the red the cold pass named is closed on a witness that reds before and greens after, and copy_lag is back on the roster its receipt already recorded. One find is sized and unclaimed: a guard's refusal is recorded in a gitignored file, so a lap that dies takes its own red with it, and the repair reaches every guard's record rather than one scan. Patchouli's OAuth stays a custody gate, unchanged from the prior lap's close.
